{
  "body_human_readable": "### Oklahoma City Thunder Claims 2024-2025 NBA Championship Title\n\nThe Oklahoma City Thunder triumphed in the 2024-2025 NBA season, securing the championship in a thrilling seven-game series against the Indiana Pacers. This victory marks the franchise's first NBA championship since relocating to Oklahoma City and their second in franchise history, the first being in 1979 as the Seattle SuperSonics.\n\nThe hard-fought Finals concluded on June 22, 2025, with the Thunder winning the decisive Game 7 on their home court with a score of 103-91. This was the first NBA Finals to go to a Game 7 since 2016.\n\n**A Season of Dominance**\n\nThe Thunder entered the playoffs as the top seed in the Western Conference, boasting a league-best regular-season record of 68 wins and 14 losses. Their performance throughout the season was record-breaking, as they outscored opponents by an average of 12.9 points per game, the highest in NBA history.\n\n**Shai Gilgeous-Alexander Leads the Way**\n\nThunder superstar Shai Gilgeous-Alexander was a pivotal figure in their championship run. He was named the NBA Finals Most Valuable Player, averaging 30.3 points per game in the series. This capped an incredible season for Gilgeous-Alexander, who also won the regular-season MVP award and the league's scoring title.\n\nThe Indiana Pacers, the Eastern Conference champions, had an inspiring playoff run that included a record five 15-point comebacks. However, their campaign ended after a hard-fought series, which saw their star Tyrese Haliburton suffer an Achilles tendon injury in the first quarter of Game 7.",
